{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured locally with `bazel --nohome_rc test --config=embedded",
    "//internal/storage/embeddeddolt:embeddeddolt_embedded_test` -- the exact",
    "config bazel.yml's bazel-embedded tier uses (race, `-test.parallel=4`, tag",
    "filter `embedded`), run with the real committed 5-shard manifest",
    "(.github/scripts/embedded-storage-test-shards.txt) so every one of the 385",
    "top-level Test* functions (excluding TestConformance, sharded separately,",
    "and TestMain, which is not dispatched through -test.run and carries no",
    "measurable duration of its own) that existed at capture time ran exactly",
    "once (local sandboxed execution only; no remote executor or cache flags",
    "were configured for this measurement run).",
    "",
    "Each value is that top-level test's own <testcase time=...> from Bazel's",
    "generated test.xml, NOT the enclosing <testsuite time=...>, for the same",
    "reason documented in scripts/ci/embedded_cmd_test_durations.json's header",
    "(empirically, <testsuite time> is a wall-clock-since-binary-start",
    "timestamp that does not isolate a concurrently-run top-level test's own",
    "duration under -test.parallel=4, while <testcase time> matches the test",
    "binary's own `--- PASS: TestX (Ys)` line exactly). Do not switch this",
    "capture to <testsuite time> without re-verifying that relationship for the",
    "toolchain in use at the time.",
    "",
    "One originally-measured top-level function,",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts_Embedded (350.25s: 81.03s + 260.70s +",
    "8.52s for its 356/712/classic-40 subtests), was subsequently split (same",
    "F1 CI-speed pass, see ~/beads-bazel-plan/f1/impl-report.md) into 3 smaller",
    "top-level functions, one per shape:",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts356_Embedded (81.03s),",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts712_Embedded (260.70s) and",
    "TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCountsClassic40_Embedded (8.52s). Unlike the",
    "cmd tier's reconstructed split durations, these 3 are exact, not summed",
    "estimates: each new function runs exactly the one subtest whose <testcase",
    "time> is listed, from this same capture. TestLargeBatchApplyStatementCounts712_Embedded",
    "genuinely still costs ~260-300s to actually run (re-confirmed by a solo",
    "re-measurement in an isolated clone: 298.60s, consistent with the 260.70s",
    "here, unlike the cmd tier's two flagged concurrency tests -- see that file's",
    "F1 follow-up correction comment) -- it is a single pinned statement-count",
    "assertion over one indivisible ApplyBatchInTx transaction (no internal",
    "sub-cases), so unlike those two it cannot be split or shown to be a",
    "measurement artifact.",
    "",
    "F1 follow-up (coordinator item 2): rather than leave this as the tier's",
    "irreducible ~260.7s floor, it is now skipped under raceEnabled (the exact",
    "precedent TestLargeBatchApplyWallClock_Embedded set for its 1000-item",
    "shape -- the cost is race-instrumentation overhead on the Dolt engine's",
    "own internal goroutine/lock machinery, not this test's own logic), with",
    "nightly.yml's \"Embedded Dolt batch-apply suite (non-race)\" step's -run",
    "regex extended to still run the full pinned assertion every night. Its",
    "weight below is therefore set to 1.0 (negligible: a skipped subtest's own",
    "<testcase time> was observed at 0.00s; 1.0 is a small nonzero placeholder",
    "so LPT packing still orders it after truly-free slots), reflecting what",
    "this test actually costs the per-PR -race lane bazel-embedded packs for",
    "-- NOT its real non-race cost, which is still ~260-300s and is what",
    "nightly.yml exercises. Do not revert this weight to 260.7 without also",
    "reverting the raceEnabled skip in large_batch_apply_measure_test.go --",
    "the two must stay in sync.",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is the weighted average seconds-per-init over",
    "every measured test in this file (sum of all durations / sum of all",
    "inits, where inits is discover_inits_cost()'s t.Run( count proxy), used",
    "only for a brand-new test with no entry yet (see",
    "scripts/ci/gen_embedded_storage_shard_manifest.py's discover_inits_cost()).",
    "",
    "As with the proxied and cmd tiers' duration files, these are a relative",
    "weight for LPT bin-packing, not an absolute SLA: within-shard",
    "-test.parallel=4 overlap, farm noisy-neighbor effects, and future code",
    "changes all mean a shard's total packed cost is a planning estimate, not",
    "a guarantee."
  ],
